n, the state House minority leader, heads the Democratic ticket with two independents also on the ballot.\n\nEvery major race rater calls Oklahoma Solid or Safe Republican, and prediction markets give Munson roughly a 7 to 9 percent chance. The state's strong Republican lean dominates the outlook, though the divisive runoff and voter interest in change give Democrats a slim path if the GOP coalition fractures. A Republican win remains the clear expectation.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0232, "margin": -13.12}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0195, "margin": -14.0}]}